{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa4_mem_q_pi_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa4_mem_q_pi_four","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L231-L235","doc":"**`κ₄ ∈ ℚ·π⁴`** — the even-rung parity: a rational multiple of `π⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa3_mem_qsqrt3_pi_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa3_mem_qsqrt3_pi_cube","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L224-L229","doc":"**`κ₃ ∈ ℚ·√3·π³`** — the odd-rung parity: a rational multiple of `√3·π³`,\nlike `κ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa2_mem_q_pi_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa2_mem_q_pi_sq","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L217-L222","doc":"**`κ₂ ∈ ℚ·π²`** — the even-rung parity: a rational multiple of `π²`,\nwith no `√3` factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa4","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L213-L215","doc":"`κ₄ = (98/729)·π⁴` — the fourth rung (even rung: pure rational).\nNumerical Ohtsuki identification, 19 confirmed digits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa3","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L209-L211","doc":"`κ₃ = (1081/21870)·√3·π³` — the third rung (odd rung: carries `√3`).\nNumerical Ohtsuki identification, 25 confirmed digits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa2","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L205-L207","doc":"`κ₂ = (2/27)·π²` — the second even-channel rung (even rung: pure rational,\nNO `√3`). Numerical Ohtsuki identification, 30 confirmed digits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa1_mem_qsqrt3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa1_mem_qsqrt3","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L179-L185","doc":"**`κ₁ ∈ ℚ(√3)·π`** (`κ₁ = (11/108)·√3π`) — the exact even-channel observable\nleading coefficient lives in the same real quadratic field `ℚ(√3)` as the naive\nsaddle `b₁`, not merely near it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa1_eq_eleven_halves_b1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa1_eq_eleven_halves_b1","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L170-L177","doc":"**`κ₁ = (11/2)·b₁`.** The Euler–Maclaurin sum-vs-integral correction multiplies\nthe naive integral-Laplace saddle `b₁ = √3π/54` by exactly `11/2`. Pure algebra\nover the certified `laplaceB1_at_saddle` value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.ohtsukiKappa1","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L165-L168","doc":"The observable even-channel leading coefficient `κ₁ = 11·√3·π/108` (the exact\nvalue of the `[1/N]` coefficient of `log J_N(4₁)`; numerical Ohtsuki\nidentification — see the section docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.laplaceB1_saddle_mem_qsqrt3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.laplaceB1_saddle_mem_qsqrt3","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L130-L140","doc":"**The naive saddle `b₁` is a rational multiple of `√3·π` — i.e. it lives in\n`ℚ(√3)·π`** (`b₁ = (1/54)·√3π`). This is the exact arithmetic *home* of the\neven channel; it is NOT the observable action coefficient `c₁` (see the module\ndocstring's honest-scope note). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.laplaceB1_at_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.laplaceB1_at_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L112-L128","doc":"**`b₁ = √3·π/54 ∈ ℚ(√3)·π`** at the exact 4₁ exponent (`2G`) saddle data\n`(g₂, g₃, g₄) = (−2√3π, −8π², −16√3π³)`. Exact arithmetic object (the numerical\nPSLQ of #3571 was entropy-blocked; this is the exact value). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.laplaceB1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.laplaceB1","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L99-L110","doc":"The leading saddle-Laplace `1/N` coefficient as a function of the first three\nsaddle Taylor data `(g₂, g₃, g₄)`:\n`b₁ = g₄/(8 g₂²) + 5 g₃²/(24 |g₂|³)`.\n\n**Domain: `g₂ < 0`.** A Laplace `1/N` expansion exists only at a *maximum* of\nthe exponent, where the second derivative `g₂ = 2·G''(x*)` is strictly negative;\nthere `|g₂| = −g₂`, which is what the `(−g2)^3` denominator encodes. This is the\nnatural (non-misuse-prone) domain — the coefficient is meaningless at `g₂ ≥ 0`.\nThe sole call site (`laplaceB1_at_saddle`) instantiates `g₂ = −2√3π < 0`\nconcretely, so no separate hypothesis is threaded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.hessian_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.hessian_eq","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L94-L97","doc":"**The Hessian `G''(x*) = π·cot(5π/6) = −√3·π ∈ ℚ(√3)·π`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.cot_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.cot_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L90-L92","doc":"`cot(5π/6) = −√3` — the arithmetic that puts the Hessian in `ℚ(√3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.grad_saddle_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.grad_saddle_zero","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L86-L88","doc":"**Critical point:** `G'(x*) = log(2 sin(5π/6)) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.cos_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.cos_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L81-L84","doc":"`cos(5π/6) = −√3/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.sin_saddle'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.sin_saddle'","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L77-L79","doc":"`sin(5π/6) = 1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.sin_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Qsqrt3Saddle.sin_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Qsqrt3SaddleArithmetic.lean#L71-L75","doc":"At the saddle `x* = 5/6`, `2·sin(5π/6) = 1` (so `G'(x*) = log 1 = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}